            <ArticleTitle>Traumatic asphyxia and blunt cardiac injury: case report and selected review.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>325-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An unusual case is described featuring traumatic asphyxia and blunt cardiac injury. An association between these is possible but not previously described. Coronary artery contusion, malignant arrhythmias, and a normal electrocardiogram were also noted and discussed. The relevant literature was reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
